name issue_415_cross_80pct_standing_queue
describe An 800 kbps constant-rate competing flow joins a 1 Mbps bottleneck (300 ms drop-tail queue) at 20 s, leaving 200 kbps for the call: libwebrtc keeps the queue full too, so this is parity, held at libwebrtc's level (#415)
# Tester repro from #415 (commit d673ea9): the call keeps the 300 ms queue full for the rest of the call (queue over
# 200 ms 66 % of the call, 14-29 s of freezes). A full drop-tail FIFO gives a flat delay gradient, and the call's loss
# (about 7 %) holds its share by arrival rate. libwebrtc does the same (#417's compare-webrtc, seeds 1-10, @ c5f159c):
#   metric                   ours mean (min-max)      libwebrtc mean (min-max)
#   cc.queue_p95_ms          296.9 (296.5-297.2)      294.7 (294.4-294.9)
#   video.freeze_total_ms    22986 (13833-29274)      24760 (21243-28554)
#   video.freeze_count       38.9 (25-49)             38.2 (32-44)
#   video.longest_freeze_ms  1824 (1216-3116)         2233 (1555-3203)
#   video.e2e_delay_p95_ms   1659 (1188-2336)         1773 (1436-2267)
#   cc.utilization_pct       49.7 (48.6-50.9)         49.8 (48.6-50.8)
#   net.loss_pct             7.2 (5.8-8.2)            7.4 (6.5-8.1)
# No gap in the parity report. The expect lines hold the call at libwebrtc's worst seed plus about 10 %, so a change
# that makes this case worse than libwebrtc fails here; the queue itself is capped by the 300 ms buffer on both stacks.
# compare_seeds 40 (#769): A/V offset p95 and video e2e p95 swing about 200 ms from seed to seed on both stacks (a
# repair or keyframe in the full queue sets the tail), so 10 seeds can't place them. #656 (adjuster timing, as
# libwebrtc) moved single seeds without moving the mean, and seeds 1-10 then read behind by 7/10: 1230 vs 1051 and
# 1748 vs 1577, band +-151. Seeds 1-40, ours on main 5bbe59d / libwebrtc (yardstick #689, run on 6c198f4): A/V offset
# p95 1149 / 1130 (sd 204 / 193), video e2e p95 1666 / 1658 (sd 204 / 196); every metric of this scenario in band.
compare_seeds 40
duration 60s
at 0s capacity=1000kbps delay=20ms queue=300ms
at 20s cross=800kbps
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 31500
expect video.freeze_count <= 49
# Moved to < 3750 with #655 part 2 (#669; window, 2026-10-29, program.md 0.2): the frame dropper's post-rewrite
# keyframe size moves seed 1 to 3701. libwebrtc on 40 seeds (yardstick #689, run 40885055886): mean 1923, worst 3778;
# ours on main mean 1900, worst 3612. The line stays below libwebrtc's worst seed.
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 3750
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 2500
expect cc.utilization_pct > 44
expect net.loss_pct < 9
expect audio.concealed_pct < 1
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 710
